In this podcast interview, AI experts Aishwarya Reganti and Kiriti Badam discuss the fundamental shift required to build successful AI-driven products, noting that traditional software playbooks are often insufficient due to non-determinism and the agency-control trade-off. They argue that creators must navigate the unpredictability of large language models by adopting a problem-first approach rather than a hype-driven one, emphasizing that reliability is earned through iterative development. Central to their philosophy is the Continuous Calibration, Continuous Development (CCCD) framework, which advocates for starting with low-autonomy systems to build a reliable feedback loop before graduating to fully autonomous agents. Ultimately, they suggest that leadership in this era requires hands-on technical intuition and the persistence to endure the "pain" of learning, which they describe as a modern competitive moat.